  lex_floats.pcpp - Lexical compliance: float literals

  Float literals follow C++ (BNF.md sec 9): 1.5, 1. and .5, an exponent
  (1e3, 2.5e-2), a hex float (0x1.8p3 is 12), a suffix (2.5f is a float32)
  and the ' separator. 1..5 is not a float: it is 1, .. and 5, a range.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lex_floats.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\lex_floats.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    1.5 1 0.5
    1000 0.025
    hex float 12
    float32 2.5
    separator 1000.5
    range 5
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    lex_floats_err_exponent.pcpp
      an exponent with no digits (LX0005)
    lex_floats_err_overflow.pcpp
      a float no float64 holds (LX0006)
    lex_floats_err_suffix.pcpp
      a C++23 float suffix the bundled clang does not take, 1.5f32 (LX0005)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_floats;

var
  LA: array[1..5] of int32;

begin
  println("{} {} {}", 1.5, 1., .5);
  println("{} {}", 1e3, 2.5e-2);
  println("hex float {}", 0x1.8p3);
  println("float32 {}", 2.5f);
  println("separator {}", 1'000.5);
  println("range {}", len(LA));
end.
